IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `spr-part8-credits-1`

-- Tests for regulations 24 to 28 (spr-part8-credits-1.l4).
-- Expected values are decided from the text of the regulation named beside each
-- group, before running. Tax years are named by the calendar year they start in (F3).

§ `Regulation 24(2): Chapter 3 does not reach back before 6 April 2016`

#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 24(2): Chapter 3 can credit the day` (YMD 2016 4 5))
#ASSERT `regulation 24(2): Chapter 3 can credit the day` (YMD 2016 4 6)
#ASSERT `regulation 24(2): Chapter 3 can credit the day` (YMD 2020 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 24(2): Chapter 3 can credit the day` (YMD 2000 1 1))

§ `Regulation 25(3): a week is counted in the tax year in which it begins`

-- A week beginning on 5 April 2016 runs into 6 April, but is counted in 2015.
#ASSERT `regulation 25(3): the tax year in which the week falls` (YMD 2016 4 5) EQUALS 2015
#ASSERT `regulation 25(3): the tax year in which the week falls` (YMD 2016 4 6) EQUALS 2016
#ASSERT `regulation 25(3): the tax year in which the week falls` (YMD 2015 4 6) EQUALS 2015

§ `Regulation 25(1): which Chapter makes provision for the week`

#ASSERT `regulation 25(1): the Chapter that makes provision for the week` (YMD 2016 4 5) EQUALS `Chapter 2 (a pre-commencement qualifying year)`
#ASSERT `regulation 25(1): the Chapter that makes provision for the week` (YMD 2016 4 6) EQUALS `Chapter 3 (a qualifying year or a post-commencement qualifying year)`
#ASSERT `regulation 25(1): the Chapter that makes provision for the week` (YMD 2010 1 1) EQUALS `Chapter 2 (a pre-commencement qualifying year)`
#ASSERT `regulation 25(1): the Chapter that makes provision for the week` (YMD 2030 1 1) EQUALS `Chapter 3 (a qualifying year or a post-commencement qualifying year)`

§ `Regulation 25(2): credited only as much as makes the year a qualifying year`

-- credit, already held, qualifying earnings factor
#ASSERT `regulation 25(2): the amount the person is credited with` 100 4900 5000 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `regulation 25(2): the amount the person is credited with` 200 4900 5000 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `regulation 25(2): the amount the person is credited with` 100 5000 5000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `regulation 25(2): the amount the person is credited with` 100 6000 5000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `regulation 25(2): the amount the person is credited with` 3000 0 5000 EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `regulation 25(2): the amount the person is credited with` 0 0 5000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `regulation 25(2): the amount the person is credited with` 5000 0 5000 EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `regulation 25(2): the amount the person is credited with` 5001 0 5000 EQUALS 5000

§ `Regulations 26 and 27: credits for a pre-commencement qualifying year`

#ASSERT `regulation 26: the earnings or contributions credited under the 1975 Regulations` (YMD 2010 6 7) 52 EQUALS JUST 52
#ASSERT `regulation 26: the earnings or contributions credited under the 1975 Regulations` (YMD 2016 4 5) 52 EQUALS JUST 52
#ASSERT `regulation 26: the earnings or contributions credited under the 1975 Regulations` (YMD 2016 4 6) 52 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `regulation 27: the Class 3 contribution credited for parents and carers` (YMD 2010 6 7) 15.85 EQUALS JUST 15.85
#ASSERT `regulation 27: the Class 3 contribution credited for parents and carers` (YMD 2016 4 5) 15.85 EQUALS JUST 15.85
#ASSERT `regulation 27: the Class 3 contribution credited for parents and carers` (YMD 2016 4 6) 15.85 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Fixtures for regulation 28`
`forces spouse, week of 7 Jun 2010, all in order` MEANS ForcesSpouseFacts WITH
    `the first day of the week` IS YMD 2010 6 7
    `the person is a spouse or civil partner of a member of Her Majesty's forces, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State for the purposes of occupying accommodation` IS TRUE
    `the person is accompanying the member of Her Majesty's forces on an assignment outside the United Kingdom, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State` IS TRUE
    `the earnings factors of the member of Her Majesty's forces for the year` IS 12000
    `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS 5000
    `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7A, 8A, 8B or 9E of the 1975 Regulations` IS FALSE
    `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week` IS FALSE
    `an application to be credited has been received by the Secretary of State` IS TRUE
    `the application is made in respect of a past period` IS TRUE
    `the application is on a form approved by the Secretary of State, or made in a manner the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient` IS TRUE
    `the application includes the information specified by the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` IS TRUE

